url: "https://not-practicable.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the canal across Florida, from the Army survey
  of 1829 that found a ship channel through the peninsula "not practicable"
  to the act of 1990 that ended the Cross Florida Barge Canal and left a
  greenway. Eight modules with 132 passages, each read against the page image
  of a public-domain printing: congressional documents, the Congressional
  Record and hearings, statutes, the public papers of the presidents, reports
  of the Army engineers, the Geological Survey and Florida's agencies, court
  decisions, the Ship Canal Authority's own Documentary History (1936), Sidney
  Lanier's Florida (1875), and Florida newspapers. It asks who paid, who
  worked, who was asked and what was lost: the bond vote of 1935 open only to
  property owners who had paid the poll tax, the relief workers at Camp
  Roosevelt, the land condemned and never returned, the Ocklawaha valley under
  the Rodman pool, and the western end at Inglis and Lake Rousseau. With 80
  public-domain plates, 10 graphics, 17 comparisons, a timeline of 42
  stations, and a list of what is not carried and why. Companion game:
  Relief and Navigation (itch.io).
